received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init` is one of the least-enforced checks atm, so that wouldn't be unreasonable. With that said, the check *is* nice & we probably should be utilizing it, so I'd prefer to keep it around. If wrappers aren't desired, most (all?) of these can be rectified directly, they'd just be comparatively more involved. I'll try a few of those out first, and if it's too much then we can disable the diagnostic outright","created_at":"2025-01-02T14:57:09Z","updated_at":"2025-01-02T14:57:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100918#discussion_r1900960501","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100918","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1900960501"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100918#discussion_r1900960501"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100918"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1900960501/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":null,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1900461625,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1901113000","pull_request_review_id":2527970123,"id":1901113000,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5xUK6o","diff_hunk":"@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@\n #include \"core/typedefs.h\"\n \n static inline float undenormalize(volatile float f) {\n-\tunion {\n+\tunion { // NOLINT(cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init) // Replace with `bit::bit_cast` in C++20.","path":"core/math/audio_frame.h","commit_id":"fe7028a4f0f2b34e84ee372096214604efbf3833","original_commit_id":"035fcd83393d40b8cbf7d98da538457db32f437a","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Alright, got the changes in. Now there's **far** less comment clutter, though the scope was expanded to account for this. Namely:\r\n- Added dedicated float↔int bitcast unions in `math_defs.h`, so everything can call to a unified standard. Will also make their eventual replacement with the C++20 `bit::bitcast` that much easier.\r\n- Removed areas which used the above unions but are now outdated. Mostly affected `math_funcs.h`, which had workarounds for standards we no longer use.\r\n- All math constructors now explicitly define their values. This was already largely integrated in #92059, so this PR now supersedes it outright.\r\n\r\nLastly, I learned that `clangd` respects *all* pragmas for IWYU[^1], not just the ones listed in its documentation. So I updated `core/typedefs.h` & `.clangd` with the new pragmas in mind.\r\n[^1]: https://github.com/include-what-you-use/include-what-you-use/blob/master/docs/IWYUPragmas.md","created_at":"2025-01-02T17:42:49Z","updated_at":"2025-01-02T17:42:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100918#discussion_r1901113000","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100918","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1901113000"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100918#discussion_r1901113000"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100918"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1901113000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":null,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1900461625,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1910198296","pull_request_review_id":2542134258,"id":1910198296,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5x21AY","diff_hunk":"@@ -220,8 +152,8 @@ class Math {\n \tstatic _ALWAYS_INLINE_ bool is_finite(double p_val) { return isfinite(p_val); }\n \tstatic _ALWAYS_INLINE_ bool is_finite(float p_val) { return isfinite(p_val); }\n \n-\tstatic _ALWAYS_INLINE_ double abs(double g) { return absd(g); }\n-\tstatic _ALWAYS_INLINE_ float abs(float g) { return absf(g); }\n+\tstatic _ALWAYS_INLINE_ double abs(double g) { return g == 0 ? 0.0 : (g < 0 ? -g : g); }","path":"core/math/math_funcs.h","commit_id":"fe7028a4f0f2b34e84ee372096214604efbf3833","original_commit_id":"9e7d68bd4b00d69ab0f206427ef4b38e7c8e9f0b","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_